Abstract: This specification adds media features for five accessibility settings that operating systems
    offer and web pages can't see: '@media/prefers-bold-text', '@media/prefers-button-shapes',
    '@media/prefers-differentiate-without-color', '@media/prefers-on-off-labels', and
    '@media/prefers-reduced-caret-blink'. Because these settings can reveal a disability, they are protected
    media features: unless the user chooses to share a setting, pages adapt their colors, outlines,
    underlines, and patterns to it without being able to find out that it is on. Where the user shares a
    setting, pages can also change their layout, and changes are delivered late so they can't link visits.
